{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 2 complete — fix pushed for review as Gerrit change 2647 (NOT submitted, NOT closed)\n\nChange: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2647 — commit `0c7c85481fa4`,\n`rebar-ticket: ff4a-2832-def4-4e55`. Awaiting `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`.\n\n### RED → GREEN\n\nOracle: `tests/unit/test_opcert_binding_thread_propagation_ff4a.py` (4 tests), written and proven\nRED **before** any fix existed, then **held out of the fix subagent's working tree** — moved\noutside the worktree and declared off-limits, so the implementer never saw its fixtures,\nassertions, or path.\n\nBaseline: 3 failed for the right reasons, 1 control passed. The mechanism test failed with exactly\nthe proven defect — the daemon resolved `tracker/.opcert-key` instead of the bound key while still\nclaiming `principal='pinned-prod-env'`. After the fix, re-applied: **4 passed**.\n\n**Mutation check (teeth), run under a `sandbox-exec` profile denying writes outside the worktree:**\n\n| seeded defect | result |\n|---|---|\n| drop the `ctx.run` context copy (re-introduce the root cause) | mechanism test → **RED** |\n| neuter the sign-time divergence guard | guard test → **RED** |\n| both restored | **4 passed** |\n\n**Refactoring litmus:** the tests assert observable outputs (the resolved key path, the raised\nexception, AST call names for the class guard) — not private names or intermediate variables.\n\n### Replication of the original report\n\nReproduced the report end-to-end: mint a real op-cert through the **actual** `_spawn_gate_daemon`\nunder a bound signer, then verify it from a **different environment** (as the operator's CLI box\n`b8a354e0` read a cert claiming `9f1c8e42`):\n\n```\nPRE-FIX   verdict: mismatch    trust_basis: pinned_environment\n          reason : ssh-keygen -Y verify rejected signature (exit 255)\nPOST-FIX  verdict: certified   trust_basis: pinned_environment\n          reason : ssh-keygen -Y verify accepted signature for principal '9f1c8e42-PROD'\n```\n\nThe pre-fix line is the ticket's reported string verbatim. **The original report no longer\nreproduces.**\n\nWorth recording: verifying the bad cert **in the signing process** returns `certified` via\n`own_key`. The signing box can always certify its own bad cert — which is why this survived\nundetected on the box that produced it and only ever failed for someone else.\n\n### The fix\n\n- **`src/rebar/_opcert_binding.py`** — new `spawn_context_daemon(target, *, name=None)`: starts a\n  daemon thread inside a `contextvars.copy_context()` taken in the **caller**, so the `_BOUND`\n  binding survives the thread boundary. It lives in the module that owns the ContextVar.\n- **`src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py`** (`_spawn_gate_daemon`) and **`src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py`**\n  (`run_workflow`'s daemon) now spawn through it. Both dropped their now-unused\n  `import threading`.\n- **`src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py`** — new `_pinned_public_key_bodies` +\n  `_refuse_if_pinned_principal_key_mismatch`, called from `mint_opcert_record`: **refuses to mint**\n  a cert whose claimed principal is pinned in `trusted_environments.yaml` but whose signing key is\n  not one of that principal's pinned keys. `OpcertKeyUnavailable` is converted by the seam to a\n  `SigningError`, so the call site records `{signed: false}` **in band** rather than persisting a\n  cert that can never certify. **This is AC3/AC4:** the failure now surfaces at sign time, while\n  the result is still in hand and free to re-sign.\n\nSafety of the guard, checked against real data: the pinned prod key\n`…hODF4VqLirMIUNFpobZZ` is exactly the key the 60 healthy sync-path certs used, so the guard is a\nno-op on every currently-working path. An **unpinned** principal (every ordinary dev box) is a\ncomplete no-op, and an absent/unreadable/malformed pin file cannot wedge signing. Keys compare on\n`\"<type> <base64>\"`, ignoring the comment field, the way `ssh` compares `allowed_signers`.\n\n### Scope & safety\n\n- **Caller-dependency sweep:** `spawn_context_daemon` is new (no callers to break). The two\n  converted call sites keep identical signatures and semantics — only the thread's starting\n  context changes. `_warn_if_verify_cannot_resolve` is untouched. Only-incidental usage; gate clear.\n- **Restoration, not creation:** no new entry point, command, or user-visible artifact. The guard\n  restores the invariant \"a minted cert verifies\".\n- **No new dependency:** `contextvars` and `threading` are stdlib.\n- **No test weakened:** one pre-existing test changed —\n  `test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py::test_unregistered_key_cert_is_rejected` mints exactly the cert\n  the new guard forbids, to exercise the **verify**-side rejection. Its `_write_trusted_env` call\n  moved to after the mint, passing the same pre-mint `era_position`, so the config the verify walk\n  reads is byte-identical. No assertion removed, weakened, or relaxed; no skip/xfail added.\n- **Gates:** `make lint` passed with **complexity `new=0 increased=0`** and **mechanism\n  `new=0`**; `make typecheck` clean (762 files). Targeted tests: the fixer ran 188 across 21\n  op-cert/MCP files, plus 29 more here. `make verify` was deliberately **not** run (host load);\n  CI's `Verified` vote is the authoritative full-suite result.\n\n### Step 7 sweep\n\n- **Construct axis:** swept every `threading.Thread(` in `src/rebar`. Ten other sites — the\n  reconciler heartbeat, snapshot janitor, doctor probe, workflow editor/snapshot/preview, eval\n  corpus feeder, and `_mcp_serving`'s uvicorn thread — none mints an op-cert.\n  `_mcp_serving` is the sanctioned exception: it **enters** `bound_signer` inside its own thread\n  target, so it needs no inherited context. One genuine sibling found (`run_workflow`) and fixed.\n- **Parity axis:** rule — *a background thread that may run a certified op must carry the signing\n  binding*. Census: **CLI** N/A (no daemon; signs in-process). **MCP async gate** — was MISSING,\n  fixed. **MCP `run_workflow`** — was MISSING, fixed. **Library** N/A. **op-cert gate service**\n  — holds (`opcert_service/jobs.py:96` enters `bound_signer` inside its own worker). A structural\n  class guard now fails the build if any `_mcp_*.py` other than `_mcp_serving.py` calls `Thread(…)`\n  again.\n\n### Attribution\n\n`caused_by → d80d-7be7-1c0a-4231` is **recorded**. Detail in the RCA comment above.\n\n### Residual risk\n\n1. **46 tickets already hold unverifiable attestations** (39 with no good cert from that\n   principal; plan-review 39, completion-verifier 20). This change stops new ones; it does not\n   repair existing ones. `rebar sign-review <id>` remains the free remedy per ticket. **Accepted —\n   surfaced for the operator's decision** on whether a backfill is wanted.\n2. **`caused_by` refused through MCP** → filed `009f-5f7f-07a5-4b36`\n   (*ambitious-creative-ovenbird*), linked `discovered_from`. The MCP container's blobless code\n   clone cannot resolve the referencing commit, so a correct attribution is unrecordable through\n   the sanctioned surface and the message points at `--force`.\n3. **AC5 not done in this change** → filed `3f5a-2ea8-7041-42a6`\n   (*slowwitted-aspherical-fireant*), linked `discovered_from`, with a sharper fix than a reorder:\n   branch the remedy on the verdict. A `mismatch` **proves** a signature was persisted, so\n   `sign-review` is unambiguously correct there; only `unsigned` is genuinely ambiguous, which is\n   what bug 94a3's both-remedies hedge was actually for.\n\n### AC status\n\nAC1 proven (runtime + store evidence) · AC2 audited (82/4797; 81 this defect; 46 tickets) ·\nAC3 sign-time refusal · AC4 defect-seeded, mutation-verified · AC5 deferred to\n`3f5a-2ea8-7041-42a6`.\n\n**Not submitted and not closed** — per the operator's instruction, pending both Gerrit votes."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788571542156927900,"uuid":"d29431ee-c530-458c-9bb3-2ca493ef521d"}